-- Plan 55 §3 case 5: a local `test`, refused.
--
-- This fixture exists because **the thing being prevented is silent**. A
-- nested `#[test]` is not collected: plan 55 §1.5 measured rustc warning
-- `cannot test inner items`, the harness running one test where two were
-- written, and the build exiting 0 regardless. Lowering this would ship a
-- test that compiles, reads as covering `add`, and never runs — so the only
-- durable record of the carve-out is a corpus entry that asserts the refusal.
--
-- `RDX0102` *"expected an expression"* was what this printed before leaf 6,
-- twice over: once on the `test` keyword from `prefix`'s default arm and
-- again on the indented body line. A refusal that does not say why is not
-- much better than no refusal, which is what `RDX0112` fixes.
--
-- The remedy is the left margin. Plan 55 §9 decision 2 declined the other
-- option, hoisting to module scope at emission, because AGENTS.md already
-- puts public-API tests in `crates/<crate>/tests/` and reserves inline tests
-- for private constructs — so co-location inside a body is a shape the
-- conventions discourage, and building hoisting for it would be cost against
-- a convention.
add : i32 -> i32 -> i32
add a b = a + b

main : ()
main =
  test "adds two numbers"
    assert add 1 2 == 3
  print "{add 1 2}"
